<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling (Homo sapiens and Mus musculus coronal, sagittal and lambdoid calvarial skull sutures)" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-5> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens and Mus musculus coronal, sagittal and lambdoid calvarial skull sutures" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A finite-element solution of masticatory strain on a CT-derived 3D skull mesh, trabecular diploe micro-CT fracture mechanics, membrane equilibrium of a pressurised triaxial ellipsoidal shell, or single-cell scRNA-seq trajectories of Twist1+/Runx2+ suture stem cells",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated CV calvarial segmentation, sagittal suture midline cleft extraction, SII (2.6791) and 5-scale dyadic box-counting fractal dimension (D_f = 1.2847) on human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg; 5 Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pseudo-spectral integrating-factor / ETDRK2 Kuramoto-Sivashinsky + KPZ solver with spatially heterogeneous alpha(x) = alpha_mean + alpha_dev(x) (alpha_dev h_xx evaluated in real space, 2/3 dealiased), a 5-layer ectocranial-to-endocranial stack through T = 6 mm coupled by explicit kappa_z d^2h/dz^2, a continuous flat/infant/overhang blend of the 2D front construction, 5 vendored regimes, a simulated 15x15 (alpha, beta) morphospace, depth ablations (no gradient, kappa_z = 0) and a nuchal : temporalis traction sweep",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Reduced-order Kirchhoff-Love vault strain field: analytic ellipsoid (90 x 70 x 65 mm), Gaussian temporalis and nuchal normal-deflection patches, isotropic intracranial membrane strain, curvature tensor projected on each suture's in-plane normal, eps_nn(s, zeta) = eps_mem + zeta kappa_nn, affine mechanotransduction alpha(eps_hat) = -0.35 + 1.55 eps_hat anchored on the vendored unloading and sagittal regimes",
        "reported_in_source: Byron et al. (2004) Anat. Rec. 279A:676-684 increased temporalis mass / bite force raises sagittal suture fractal dimension (direction of mechanotransduction only); Herring & Teng (2000) in vivo suture strains are suture-specific and heterogeneous; Curtis et al. (2013) full-skull finite-element suture-strain coupling (precedent, not reproduced)",
        "reported_in_source: Jaslow (1990) J. Biomech. 23:313-321 monotonic enhancement of cranial suture bending and impact energy absorption with Suture Interdigitation Index SII = L_arc / L_chord",
        "reported_in_source: Khonsari et al. (2013) Proc. R. Soc. B 280:20122670 & Zollikofer & Weissmann (2011) J. Anat. 219:100-114 bidirectional normal-front overhang and FGFR2 craniosynostosis fusion",
        "reported_in_source: Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106:11218-11223 fourth-order Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ osteogenic front instability dh/dt = -alpha*d^2h/dx^2 - beta*d^4h/dx^4 + (v_0/2)*(dh/dx)^2 + eta(x,t) generating self-affine fractal cranial suture interdigitation (D_f ~ 1.30-1.45) and collapse to a flat line under surgical mechanical unloading",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D/2D osteogenic front geometry (x(s), y(s)), box-counting D_f, SII and Jaslow bending energy ratio compared against the superior-view human calvarial sagittal suture only; coronal, lambdoid and endocranial outputs are compared against vendored/literature expectations, not against a specimen",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2D overhanging trace is a phenomenological construction (std(h)-normalised KS shape plus cascade harmonics), so D_f/SII magnitudes are set by that construction rather than by the PDE amplitude",
        "transfer_boundary: The strain field is a reduced-order analytic model whose traction magnitudes are stated assumptions; it reproduces the mean-alpha ordering lambdoid > sagittal > coronal but NOT the SII ordering (lambdoid/sagittal SII = 0.885 vs vendored 1.22) for any nuchal scale in [0, 2]" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Morphogen gradient & pre-cartilage condensation zone in Homo sapiens" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
