<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the module docstring maps Laws 1-5 to Lean theorem names and code; `strain_to_alpha`, `calvarial_shell_strain_field`, `construct_osteogenic_front_curve` and `simulate_cranial_suture_regime` docstrings state the equation, the source figure and the honest scope; the math-KG loop file registers all 5 laws with corrected code loci (L1-167). Deductions: the Gaussian-deflection Hessian form, the isotropic ICP membrane term and the overhang law are modelling choices with no cited equation (L284-289, L322-344) (-6); the cascade harmonic coefficients remain uncited (L483-488) (-4); the self-test docstring and panel B1 now say \"5 dyadic scales\" (the v2 \"7-scale\" wording was wrong and is fixed) (+0)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py L284–L289: overhang_from_alpha: uncited 0.68 (alpha/1.2)^0.7 closure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L284-L289>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the damped KS dispersion and completing-the-square identity (L126-136, L203-262), the pseudo-spectral integrating-factor step with 2/3 dealiasing, the new heterogeneous-alpha treatment (alpha_mean in the exact integrating factor, -alpha_dev(x) h_xx in real space, L616-631), the 5-layer through-plate stack with explicit Neumann kappa_z coupling (L634-637), the Kirchhoff-Love eps(zeta) = eps_mem + zeta kappa law and the affine mechanotransduction law anchored on the two vendored regimes (L267-281, L346-441), all with 5 machine-checked Lean theorems; the constant-profile case reduces bitwise to the Pass 2 solver (self-test 9). Deductions: the 2D overhanging front is not a solved bidirectional interface — `construct_osteogenic_front_curve` normalises the KS field by std(h) and adds three hand-coded cascade harmonics and a lobe drive locked to h, so only the shape (not the amplitude) of the PDE solution reaches D_f/SII (L466-491; -8); the vault strain field is Gaussian deflection patches plus an isotropic ICP term, not a shell-equilibrium or finite-element solution, and the lambdoid asterion flanks need an alpha clip of 3.0 to keep the explicit term stable (L322-344, L368, JSON L151; -5); the integrating factor is clipped to [-4, 0.12] and the growth saturation 1/(1 + 0.55 var h) and cubic -0.18 h^3 are uncited closures (L619, L629-632; -3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py L466–L491: Carried defect: trace amplitude normalised by std(h) and cascade harmonics 0.62/0.34/0.16 hand-coded; D_f/SII are set by this construction, not by the PDE amplitude <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L466-L491>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: 11 measurements each with a reference value, source and note (L1295-1427): sagittal D_f 1.3484 vs 1.36, SII 2.9181 vs 2.84, lambdoid D_f 1.3756 vs 1.41, synostosis collapse 1.00, Jaslow amplification 2.687 vs 2.75, specimen CV D_f 1.2847, ecto/endo SII ratio 2.863 vs null 1.0 with ablation values, strain-coupled lambdoid/sagittal SII 0.885 vs vendored 1.22 (a disclosed failure), nuchal crossing scale 0.5, alpha(0) = -0.35 exactly, morphospace rho = 1.00. Deductions: the new references for items 7-9 are a null value (1.0), a vendored expectation (1.22) and a model assumption (1.0) rather than numbers measured on real specimens; no quantified ecto/endo D_f pair from the literature is vendored (-7); the lambdoid/sagittal comparison fails and is only explained qualitatively (-4); Spearman is computed with a ties-unaware argsort (L762, L851) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py L1387–L1396: Strain-coupled lambdoid/sagittal SII 0.885 vs reference 1.22: disclosed mismatch <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L1387-L1396>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-adult-lambdoid-suture-hyper-interdigitated-fractal-dimension-d-f>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-adult-sagittal-suture-box-counting-fractal-dimension-d-f>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-adult-sagittal-suture-interdigitation-index-sii-l-arc-l-chord>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-ectocranial-endocranial-sagittal-sii-ratio-across-the-quasi-3d-plate-thickness-pass-3-item-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-fgfr2-apert-craniosynostosis-mechanical-unloading-sii-collapse-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-human-calvaria-specimen-sagittal-suture-cv-box-counting-fractal-dimension-d-f>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-jaslow-1990-bending-energy-absorption-amplification-factor-lambdoid-vs-fused-synostosis>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-nuchal-temporalis-traction-scale-at-which-mean-ectocranial-lambdoid-alpha-first-exceeds-sagittal-alpha-sensitivity-of-the-assumed-ordering>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-simulated-alpha-beta-morphospace-spearman-rank-correlation-of-d-f-with-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-strain-coupled-lambdoid-sagittal-sii-ratio-under-heterogeneous-masticatory-strain-pass-3-item-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-measurement-strain-mechanotransduction-law-alpha-at-zero-strain-miura-2009-unloading-reproduction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — MorphoEval overall 86.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 closes both v2 remediation items in reduced, explicitly labelled form and re-scores the script at 86.5/100 (down from 92.4). The solver now integrates a spatially heterogeneous alpha(x) Kuramoto-Sivashinsky/KPZ front in a 5-layer ectocranial-to-endocranial stack (`simulate_cranial_suture_regime`, L505-727) and derives alpha(s, zeta) for the coronal, sagittal and lambdoid sutures from a reduced-order Kirchhoff-Love vault strain field (`calvarial_shell_strain_field`, L346-441) through an affine mechanotransduction law (`strain_to_alpha`, L267-281) formalised by two new Lean 4 theorems. Results: ectocranial sagittal SII 2.863 / D_f 1.339 against a flat endocranial table (SII 1.000; no-gradient null 2.81, kappa_z = 0 ablation 1.00), strain-coupled SII coronal 2.161 < lambdoid 2.433 < sagittal 2.748, simulated morphospace Spearman rho(D_f, alpha) = 1.00 and rho(D_f, beta) = -1.00, the five vendored regimes and the GIF numerically unchanged (sagittal D_f 1.3484, SII 2.9181; specimen CV D_f 1.2847, SII 2.6791). The score falls because the round exposed that the 2D overhang trace is a std(h)-normalised phenomenological construction, that the reduced strain model fails the lambdoid > sagittal SII comparison, and that only the sagittal suture is validated against a specimen. Overall 86.5/100 (faithfulness 84.6, reproducibility 90.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/allometric_cranial_sutures_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py at d58a084, image/png, 1553683 B, 2227×2349 px, artifact_sha256 7d403d848e058ca7d287c7643ecb7c7794378d0d5755d61934ce8ee7cc788cf8 (sha256 7d403d848e058ca7d287c7643ecb7c7794378d0d5755d61934ce8ee7cc788cf8), spec_fingerprint 74cdd6073c2c17e25ba7d52bc092caa9009007cab52635bb5182e43bad1f6297. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 74cdd6073c2c17e25ba7d52bc092caa9009007cab52635bb5182e43bad1f6297; artifact_sha256: 7d403d848e058ca7d287c7643ecb7c7794378d0d5755d61934ce8ee7cc788cf8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/allometric_cranial_sutures_reference.json=c41074e16d3025c9..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg=b3c411a6a4713770..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/paper_citations.bib=81d1b1b367ddb12c..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/scout_manifest.json=226c072307597439...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-allometric-cranial-sutures-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106:11218-11223 fourth-order Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ osteogenic front instability dh/dt = -alpha*d^2h/dx^2 - beta*d^4h/dx^4 + (v_0/2)*(dh/dx)^2 + eta(x,t) generating self-affine fractal cranial suture interdigitation (D_f ~ 1.30-1.45) and collapse to a flat line under surgical mechanical unloading | Jaslow (1990) J. Biomech. 23:313-321 monotonic enhancement of cranial suture bending and impact energy absorption with Suture Interdigitation Index SII = L_arc / L_chord | Khonsari et al. (2013) Proc. R. Soc. B 280:20122670 & Zollikofer & Weissmann (2011) J. Anat. 219:100-114 bidirectional normal-front overhang and FGFR2 craniosynostosis fusion | Byron et al. (2004) Anat. Rec. 279A:676-684 increased temporalis mass / bite force raises sagittal suture fractal dimension (direction of mechanotransduction only); Herring & Teng (2000) in vivo suture strains are suture-specific and heterogeneous; Curtis et al. (2013) full-skull finite-element suture-strain coupling (precedent, not reproduced); reconstructed_in_script: Pseudo-spectral integrating-factor / ETDRK2 Kuramoto-Sivashinsky + KPZ solver with spatially heterogeneous alpha(x) = alpha_mean + alpha_dev(x) (alpha_dev h_xx evaluated in real space, 2/3 dealiased), a 5-layer ectocranial-to-endocranial stack through T = 6 mm coupled by explicit kappa_z d^2h/dz^2, a continuous flat/infant/overhang blend of the 2D front construction, 5 vendored regimes, a simulated 15x15 (alpha, beta) morphospace, depth ablations (no gradient, kappa_z = 0) and a nuchal : temporalis traction sweep | Reduced-order Kirchhoff-Love vault strain field: analytic ellipsoid (90 x 70 x 65 mm), Gaussian temporalis and nuchal normal-deflection patches, isotropic intracranial membrane strain, curvature tensor projected on each suture's in-plane normal, eps_nn(s, zeta) = eps_mem + zeta kappa_nn, affine mechanotransduction alpha(eps_hat) = -0.35 + 1.55 eps_hat anchored on the vendored unloading and sagittal regimes | Automated CV calvarial segmentation, sagittal suture midline cleft extraction, SII (2.6791) and 5-scale dyadic box-counting fractal dimension (D_f = 1.2847) on human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg; 5 Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys); transfer_boundary: 1D/2D osteogenic front geometry (x(s), y(s)), box-counting D_f, SII and Jaslow bending energy ratio compared against the superior-view human calvarial sagittal suture only; coronal, lambdoid and endocranial outputs are compared against vendored/literature expectations, not against a specimen | The strain field is a reduced-order analytic model whose traction magnitudes are stated assumptions; it reproduces the mean-alpha ordering lambdoid > sagittal > coronal but NOT the SII ordering (lambdoid/sagittal SII = 0.885 vs vendored 1.22) for any nuchal scale in [0, 2] | The 2D overhanging trace is a phenomenological construction (std(h)-normalised KS shape plus cascade harmonics), so D_f/SII magnitudes are set by that construction rather than by the PDE amplitude; does_not_claim: A finite-element solution of masticatory strain on a CT-derived 3D skull mesh, trabecular diploe micro-CT fracture mechanics, membrane equilibrium of a pressurised triaxial ellipsoidal shell, or single-cell scRNA-seq trajectories of Twist1+/Runx2+ suture stem cells." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py:322-344 and 386-389 with datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/allometric_cranial_sutures_reference.json:135-180 — the vault strain is Gaussian deflection Hessians plus an isotropic ICP term; it fails the lambdoid > sagittal SII comparison (0.885 vs 1.22) for every nuchal scale in the sweep. Implement a thin-shell (Koiter/Kirchhoff-Love) finite-difference or FEM solve with membrane equilibrium on the ellipsoid (or vendor an open CT skull mesh) and re-run the three-suture comparison.",
        "remediation needed: 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py:466-491 — `construct_osteogenic_front_curve` normalises the KS field by std(h) (L471, L479, L483) and adds hand-coded cascade harmonics (0.62/0.34/0.16) and a lobe drive, so D_f and SII are set by the construction rather than by the PDE amplitude. Replace with a solved bidirectional interface (Zollikofer & Weissmann 2011 two-front growth or a 2D phase-field level set) whose overhang emerges from normal growth, and let the KS amplitude propagate.",
        "remediation needed: 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py:762-768 and 851-853 — Spearman correlations use a ties-unaware argsort-of-argsort, which is why the depth profile reports -0.90 rather than -1.0 for a monotone profile with two saturated layers. Use `scipy.stats.spearmanr` and add a tie-aware monotonicity test.",
        "remediation needed: 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py:893-913 — only the sagittal suture is extractable from the vendored photograph. Vendor a CC-licensed lateral/posterior view (coronal + lambdoid in frame) and an endocranial view, extend `segment_human_suture_specimen` to arbitrary oriented ROIs, and turn measurements 7-8 into specimen comparisons instead of null/vendored references.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/allometric_cranial_sutures_reference.json:151 and 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py:616-631 — the explicit -alpha_dev(x) h_xx term needs an alpha clip of 3.0 for stability and the clip changes the lambdoid mean alpha (2.0 -> 1.06, 3.0 -> 1.27). Treat the heterogeneous term implicitly (IMEX / Crank-Nicolson on alpha(x) k^2) so no clip is required, and report the lambdoid profile unclipped." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.65e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the morphospace is now 225 real simulations and is monotone (Spearman rho(D_f, alpha) = 1.00, rho(SII, alpha) = 1.00, rho(D_f, beta | unstable) = -1.00, flat half-plane max D_f 1.00; L728-781, self-test 14); the depth ramp alpha_endo_ratio and kappa_z each have an ablation (L814-859); the nuchal : temporalis scale is swept (L861-888); the continuous flat/infant/overhang blend (L498-501) makes intermediate alphas vary smoothly. Deductions: within the sweep the nuchal scale changes the mean-alpha ratio (0.98 -> 1.10) but never flips the SII ordering (0.80-0.88), so the lambdoid-vs-sagittal feature of form is not controllable by the one strain parameter that is exposed (-6); the alpha clip 3.0 and the overhang law 0.68 (alpha/1.2)^0.7 (L284-289) are uncited knobs that shape the response (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py L861–L888: Nuchal traction sweep recording alpha and SII ratios; SII ratio stays < 1 for all scales <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L861-L888>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: cross-process determinism (seed + SHA-256 label offsets, L551-553), bitwise two-run and constant-profile equivalence checks, 14-check `--self-test` in ~3 s, default render in ~14 s with `--skip-gif`/`--seed` flags (L1542-1546), SHA-256 fail-closed inputs, and the GIF regenerating byte-identically to v2 (27e6d90f...). Deductions: no per-script requirements lock (environment is recorded only in this audit) (-5); matplotlib needs a writable MPLCONFIGDIR in sandboxed runs and the invocation notes do not say so (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
