        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — Source and data traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: 8 DOIs (4 primary + 4 Pass 3 secondary, each resolved against Crossref before being added) in the bib, dataset README and JSON; the bib SHA-256 was re-pinned after the additions and is verified fail-closed at every run (L107-120); every strain-model constant lives in `calvarial_shell_strain_model` with `not_a_finite_element_model: true`, a `used_for` line per secondary reference and explicit \"assumption\" wording. Deductions: the ecto-vs-endo expectation cites Nicolay & Vaders (2006) qualitatively without a vendored table value (-4); the ellipsoid semi-axes, plate thickness 6 mm, patch centres and sigma values carry no anatomical source (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
