        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation, Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability, quasi-3D plate layering and reduced-order masticatory strain coupling — Morphological realism / specimen match: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the SHA-256-pinned CC BY-SA human calvaria is segmented, its sagittal suture traced and overlaid (C1), compared waveform-to-waveform (C2) and in box-counting space (B1) with the simulated sagittal suture, and the five regimes are visually distinct (A1, GIF); the new row D shows the ellipsoidal vault with the three suture paths, the heterogeneous alpha(s) profiles and the quasi-3D ecto-to-endo cleft stack with a clearly flatter endocranial table, which is the qualitative anatomy. Deductions: the coronal, lambdoid and endocranial outputs have no specimen counterpart — the vendored photograph shows only the sagittal suture fully in frame (L893-897, L913) (-8); the strain-coupled lambdoid is LESS interdigitated than the sagittal (SII 2.433 vs 2.748), opposite to the vendored/literature expectation, so the three-suture rendering does not match adult human morphology in that respect (-6); the vault is an analytic ellipsoid without temporal squama, occipital bun or thickness variation, and the muscle patches are four points (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

