<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) Kuramoto-Sivashinsky Osteogenic Front Dispersion & Peak Wavenumber Selection Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the fourth-order Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic dispersion relation selects a unique most-unstable interdigitation wavenumber q_max = alpha/(2*beta) with strictly positive peak growth rate omega_max = alpha^2/(4*beta) > 0 | Variables: q = k^2 >= 0: squared spatial wavenumber along the suture midline; alpha > 0: BMP4/FGF2 + tensile strain osteogenic front instability coefficient; beta > 0: fourth-order surface-tension / curvature smoothing coefficient" ;
    dct:source "Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106(27):11218-11223 Figs. 2-4; Zollikofer & Weissmann (2011) J. Anat. 219:100-114" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L126-L262>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean#L20-L56> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def sq_int (z : Int) : Int :=
  z * z
def ks_dispersion (alpha beta q : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * q - beta * q * q
def ks_scaled_lhs (alpha beta q : Int) : Int :=
  4 * beta * ks_dispersion alpha beta q + sq_int (2 * beta * q - alpha)
theorem ks_dispersion_peak_selection (alpha : Int) :
    ks_dispersion alpha 0 0 = 0 ∧
    ks_scaled_lhs 12 6 1 = sq_int 12 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 1 = 6 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 0 = 0 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 2 = 0 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 1 > ks_dispersion 12 6 0 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 1 > ks_dispersion 12 6 2 ∧
    sq_int 15 > sq_int 12 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [ks_dispersion]
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "omega(q) = alpha * q - beta * q^2 (q = k^2);   4 * beta * omega(q) + (2 * beta * q - alpha)^2 = alpha^2;   q_max = alpha / (2 * beta)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/1096-8644(200008)112:4%3C575::AID-AJPA10%3E3.0.CO;2-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.a.20055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jmor.10445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9290(90)90059-C>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0813269106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2013.0442>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2012.2670>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2011.01386.x> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cranial Suture Fractal Interdigitation & Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ Osteogenic Front Instability" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.ks_dispersion" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.ks_dispersion_peak_selection" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mechanical Unloading & FGFR2 Apert Craniosynostosis Flat Suture Stability Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that removing tensile mechanical strain (Miura et al. 2009 unloading experiment) or premature osteoblast differentiation in FGFR2 craniosynostosis (alpha <= 0) makes all spatial Fourier modes decay (omega(q) <= 0), collapsing the suture into a flat or fused line (D_f -> 1.0, SII -> 1.0) | Variables: alpha <= 0: stabilized osteogenic front under surgical mechanical unloading or FGFR2 gain-of-function craniosynostosis; gamma >= 0: mesenchymal confinement damping" ;
    dct:source "Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106:11218-11223 Fig. 5; Khonsari et al. (2013) Proc. R. Soc. B 280:20122670" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L505-L727>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean#L59-L83> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ks_damped_dispersion (alpha beta gamma q : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * q - beta * q * q - gamma
theorem unloaded_and_craniosynostosis_flat_stability (gamma : Int) (hgamma : gamma ≥ 0) :
    ks_damped_dispersion 0 6 gamma 0 ≤ 0 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-35) 60 8 1 = -103 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-35) 60 8 2 = -318 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-60) 80 25 1 = -165 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-60) 80 25 2 = -465 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion 120 60 4 1 = 56 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · dsimp [ks_damped_dispersion]
    omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "alpha <= 0, beta >= 0, gamma >= 0, q = k^2 >= 0  ==>  omega(q) = alpha * q - beta * q^2 - gamma <= 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/1096-8644(200008)112:4%3C575::AID-AJPA10%3E3.0.CO;2-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.a.20055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jmor.10445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9290(90)90059-C>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0813269106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2013.0442>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2012.2670>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2011.01386.x> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cranial Suture Fractal Interdigitation & Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ Osteogenic Front Instability" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.ks_damped_dispersion" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.unloaded_and_craniosynostosis_flat_stability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jaslow (1990) Suture Interdigitation Index (SII) & Bending Energy Absorption Hierarchy Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that fractal interdigitation amplifies dynamic impact and bending energy absorption monotonically across fused FGFR2 craniosynostosis (SII=1.00) < neonatal infant suture (SII=1.06) < adult sagittal suture (SII=2.84) < adult lambdoid suture (SII=3.48) | Variables: SII = L_arc / L_chord: ratio of interdigitated suture arc length to straight midline chord length; E_0: flat-suture baseline bending energy; kappa_J = 0.72: Jaslow (1990) interdigitation energy absorption slope" ;
    dct:source "Jaslow (1990) J. Biomech. 23(4):313-321 Figs. 2-5; Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106:11218-11223" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L138-L201>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean#L86-L116> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def jaslow_energy_100 (e0 kappa_100 sii_100 : Int) : Int :=
  e0 * (10000 + kappa_100 * (sii_100 - 100))
theorem jaslow_suture_interdigitation_energy_absorption (e0 kappa_100 : Int) :
    jaslow_energy_100 e0 kappa_100 100 = e0 * 10000 ∧
    jaslow_energy_100 10 72 100 = 100000 ∧
    jaslow_energy_100 10 72 106 = 104320 ∧
    jaslow_energy_100 10 72 284 = 232480 ∧
    jaslow_energy_100 10 72 348 = 278560 ∧
    jaslow_energy_100 10 72 100 < jaslow_energy_100 10 72 106 ∧
    jaslow_energy_100 10 72 106 < jaslow_energy_100 10 72 284 ∧
    jaslow_energy_100 10 72 284 < jaslow_energy_100 10 72 348 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [jaslow_energy_100]
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "SII = L_arc / L_chord >= 1.0;   E_bend(SII) = E_0 * (1 + kappa_J * (SII - 1.0));   SII_lambdoid > SII_sagittal > SII_infant > SII_fused = 1.0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/1096-8644(200008)112:4%3C575::AID-AJPA10%3E3.0.CO;2-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.a.20055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jmor.10445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9290(90)90059-C>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0813269106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2013.0442>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2012.2670>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2011.01386.x> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cranial Suture Fractal Interdigitation & Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ Osteogenic Front Instability" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.jaslow_energy_100" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.jaslow_suture_interdigitation_energy_absorption" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Strain Mechanotransduction Law: Osteogenic Instability alpha as an Affine Function of Normalised Tensile Suture Strain (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Couples the reduced-order masticatory strain tensor to the KS osteogenic instability so that alpha(s, zeta) is spatially heterogeneous along each suture and through the plate; reproduces the unloading and sagittal regimes as its two anchor points and is strictly monotone (Byron et al. 2004 direction) | Variables: eps_hat: tensile strain normal to the suture divided by the ectocranial sagittal mean (dimensionless); alpha_unl = -0.35: vendored unloaded-null instability; alpha_sag = 1.20: vendored adult sagittal instability; eps_hat_c = 0.2258: zero crossing below which omega(k) <= 0 (Law 2)" ;
    dct:source "Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106:11218-11223 Fig. 5 (unloading); Byron et al. (2004) Anat. Rec. 279A:676-684; Herring & Teng (2000) Am. J. Phys. Anthropol. 112:575-593" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L267-L441>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean#L117-L157> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def alpha_of_strain (a_unl a_sag eps_1000 : Int) : Int :=
  1000 * a_unl + (a_sag - a_unl) * eps_1000
theorem strain_mechanotransduction_alpha_monotone (a_unl a_sag e1 e2 : Int)
    (hgain : a_unl < a_sag) (hlt : e1 < e2) :
    alpha_of_strain a_unl a_sag 0 = 1000 * a_unl ∧
    alpha_of_strain a_unl a_sag 1000 = 1000 * a_sag ∧
    alpha_of_strain a_unl a_sag e1 < alpha_of_strain a_unl a_sag e2 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 0 = -35000 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 1000 = 120000 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 225 = -125 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 226 = 30 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 0 < 0 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 1000 > 0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [alpha_of_strain]
  · unfold alpha_of_strain
    omega
  · unfold alpha_of_strain
    have hpos : 0 < a_sag - a_unl := Int.sub_pos.mpr hgain
    have hmul : (a_sag - a_unl) * e1 < (a_sag - a_unl) * e2 := Int.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left hlt hpos
    omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "alpha(eps_hat) = alpha_unl + (alpha_sag - alpha_unl) * eps_hat;   alpha(0) = alpha_unl = -0.35 (Miura 2009 unloading);   alpha(1) = alpha_sag = 1.20;   d alpha / d eps_hat = alpha_sag - alpha_unl > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/1096-8644(200008)112:4%3C575::AID-AJPA10%3E3.0.CO;2-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.a.20055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jmor.10445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9290(90)90059-C>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0813269106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2013.0442>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2012.2670>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2011.01386.x> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cranial Suture Fractal Interdigitation & Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ Osteogenic Front Instability" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.alpha_of_strain" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.strain_mechanotransduction_alpha_monotone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kirchhoff-Love Through-Thickness Strain & Ectocranial > Endocranial Suture Instability Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Gives the quasi-3D plate layering its depth law: the ectocranial table is the most tensile and most unstable layer and the endocranial table is compressive (alpha ~ -0.50, flat by Law 2), so endocranial sutures remain simpler than ectocranial traces in the 5-layer KS stack coupled by kappa_z d^2h/dz^2 | Variables: eps_mem = 0.45: isotropic intracranial-pressure membrane strain (normalised); kappa_nn: vault-flattening curvature change along the in-plane suture normal from Gaussian muscle deflection patches; zeta: through-thickness offset, ectocranial +T/2 = +3 mm, endocranial -T/2 = -3 mm (T = 6 mm)" ;
    dct:source "Nicolay & Vaders (2006) J. Morphol. 267:841-849 (ecto vs endo suture complexity, qualitative); Curtis et al. (2013) J. R. Soc. Interface 10:20130442 (FEM precedent, not reproduced); Herring & Teng (2000)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L346-L441,L505-L727,L814-L859>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean#L159-L193> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def through_thickness_strain (eps_mem kappa zeta : Int) : Int :=
  eps_mem + zeta * kappa
theorem kirchhoff_love_ectocranial_endocranial_ordering (eps_mem kappa t_half : Int)
    (hk : 0 < kappa) (ht : 0 < t_half) :
    through_thickness_strain eps_mem kappa 0 = eps_mem ∧
    through_thickness_strain eps_mem kappa (-t_half) < through_thickness_strain eps_mem kappa t_half ∧
    through_thickness_strain 450 183 3 = 999 ∧
    through_thickness_strain 450 183 (-3) = -99 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 (through_thickness_strain 450 183 3) = 119845 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 (through_thickness_strain 450 183 (-3)) = -50345 ∧
    alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 (through_thickness_strain 450 183 (-3)) <
      alpha_of_strain (-35) 120 (through_thickness_strain 450 183 3) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [through_thickness_strain]
  · unfold through_thickness_strain
    have hpos : 0 < t_half * kappa := Int.mul_pos ht hk
    have hneg : (-t_half) * kappa = -(t_half * kappa) := Int.neg_mul t_half kappa
    omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "eps_nn(s, zeta) = eps_mem + zeta * kappa_nn(s), zeta in [-T/2, +T/2];   kappa_nn > 0, T > 0  ==>  eps_nn(+T/2) > eps_nn(-T/2)  ==>  alpha_ecto > alpha_endo (by Law 4)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/1096-8644(200008)112:4%3C575::AID-AJPA10%3E3.0.CO;2-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.a.20055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jmor.10445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9290(90)90059-C>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0813269106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2013.0442>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2012.2670>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2011.01386.x> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Cranial Suture Fractal Interdigitation & Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ Osteogenic Front Instability" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.through_thickness_strain" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.kirchhoff_love_ectocranial_endocranial_ordering" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) Kuramoto-Sivashinsky Osteogenic Front Dispersion & Peak Wavenumber Selection Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the fourth-order Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic dispersion relation selects a unique most-unstable interdigitation wavenumber q_max = alpha/(2*beta) with strictly positive peak growth rate omega_max = alpha^2/(4*beta) > 0 | Variables: q = k^2 >= 0: squared spatial wavenumber along the suture midline; alpha > 0: BMP4/FGF2 + tensile strain osteogenic front instability coefficient; beta > 0: fourth-order surface-tension / curvature smoothing coefficient" ;
    dct:source "Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106(27):11218-11223 Figs. 2-4; Zollikofer & Weissmann (2011) J. Anat. 219:100-114" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L126-L262>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean#L20-L56> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def sq_int (z : Int) : Int :=
  z * z
def ks_dispersion (alpha beta q : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * q - beta * q * q
def ks_scaled_lhs (alpha beta q : Int) : Int :=
  4 * beta * ks_dispersion alpha beta q + sq_int (2 * beta * q - alpha)
theorem ks_dispersion_peak_selection (alpha : Int) :
    ks_dispersion alpha 0 0 = 0 ∧
    ks_scaled_lhs 12 6 1 = sq_int 12 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 1 = 6 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 0 = 0 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 2 = 0 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 1 > ks_dispersion 12 6 0 ∧
    ks_dispersion 12 6 1 > ks_dispersion 12 6 2 ∧
    sq_int 15 > sq_int 12 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [ks_dispersion]
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "omega(q) = alpha * q - beta * q^2 (q = k^2);   4 * beta * omega(q) + (2 * beta * q - alpha)^2 = alpha^2;   q_max = alpha / (2 * beta)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/1096-8644(200008)112:4%3C575::AID-AJPA10%3E3.0.CO;2-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.a.20055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jmor.10445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9290(90)90059-C>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0813269106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2013.0442>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2012.2670>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2011.01386.x> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Cranial Suture Fractal Interdigitation & Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ Osteogenic Front Instability" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.ks_dispersion" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.ks_dispersion_peak_selection" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mechanical Unloading & FGFR2 Apert Craniosynostosis Flat Suture Stability Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that removing tensile mechanical strain (Miura et al. 2009 unloading experiment) or premature osteoblast differentiation in FGFR2 craniosynostosis (alpha <= 0) makes all spatial Fourier modes decay (omega(q) <= 0), collapsing the suture into a flat or fused line (D_f -> 1.0, SII -> 1.0) | Variables: alpha <= 0: stabilized osteogenic front under surgical mechanical unloading or FGFR2 gain-of-function craniosynostosis; gamma >= 0: mesenchymal confinement damping" ;
    dct:source "Miura et al. (2009) PNAS 106:11218-11223 Fig. 5; Khonsari et al. (2013) Proc. R. Soc. B 280:20122670" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py#L505-L727>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_020_allometric_cranial_sutures.lean#L59-L83> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ks_damped_dispersion (alpha beta gamma q : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * q - beta * q * q - gamma
theorem unloaded_and_craniosynostosis_flat_stability (gamma : Int) (hgamma : gamma ≥ 0) :
    ks_damped_dispersion 0 6 gamma 0 ≤ 0 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-35) 60 8 1 = -103 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-35) 60 8 2 = -318 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-60) 80 25 1 = -165 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion (-60) 80 25 2 = -465 ∧
    ks_damped_dispersion 120 60 4 1 = 56 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · dsimp [ks_damped_dispersion]
    omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "alpha <= 0, beta >= 0, gamma >= 0, q = k^2 >= 0  ==>  omega(q) = alpha * q - beta * q^2 - gamma <= 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/1096-8644(200008)112:4%3C575::AID-AJPA10%3E3.0.CO;2-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.a.20055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jmor.10445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-9290(90)90059-C>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0813269106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2013.0442>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2012.2670>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2011.01386.x> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Cranial Suture Fractal Interdigitation & Kuramoto-Sivashinsky / KPZ Osteogenic Front Instability" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.ks_damped_dispersion" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_020.unloaded_and_craniosynostosis_flat_stability" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jaslow (1990) Suture Interdigitation Index (SII) & Bending Energy Absorption Hierarchy Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that fractal interdigitation amplifies dynamic impact and bending energy absorption monotonically across fused FGFR2 craniosynostosis (SII=1.00) < neonatal infant suture (SII=1.06) < adult sagittal suture (SII=2.84) < adult lambdoid suture (SII=3.48) | Variables: SII = L_arc / L_chord: ratio of interdigitated suture arc length to straight midline chord length; E_0: flat-suture baseline bending energy; kappa_J = 0.72: Jaslow (1990) interdigitation energy absorption slope" ;
